    "rationale": "A weekend military escalation involving direct CENTCOM strikes on Iranian tankers and IRGC retaliation in the Strait of Hormuz has restricted exports and shut in 8.3 million bpd of Gulf output. This physical disruption caused WTI to climb by $1.14 (1.25%) on Monday, September 7, to settle at $92.62, higher than the latest model target observation on September 4 ($91.48) and the model point forecast of $90.89. This supports a moderate upward center shift and wider uncertainty.",
